<title>YUGOSLAVIA: Savings, stability key to Yugo fin.mkt development.</title>
<headline>Savings, stability key to Yugo fin.mkt development.</headline>
<byline>Gordana Filipovic</byline>
<dateline>BELGRADE 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yugoslavia's nascent financial markets will develop only when banks restore detained household savings and the economy stabilises, a financial expert said on Monday.</p>
<p>At present, efforts to kick start secondary trading in the financial markets have proved futile, Djordje Djukic, an economist and a member of the central bank board of governors, told Reuters.</p>
<p>&quot;The short-term securities market is illiquid and lacks volume. There is no capital market and it will take years for share and bond trading to emerge and stabilise,&quot; he said.</p>
</text>
